  "name": "Example: Finding the Pivot Columns of a Matrix in Row Echelon Form",
  "problem": "The row echelon form matrix $B$ is given below. What are its pivot columns?\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "Remember that the pivots of a matrix in row echelon form are the first non-zero entries in each row of the matrix.\n\nWe can see that $B$ has $3$ pivots in the $2$nd, $3$rd, and $4$th columns:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
